{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why","id":810904,"title":"Your Favorite Tribes: Which and Why!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-17T18:52:08-08:00","id":810904,"title":"Your Favorite Tribes: Which and Why!?","content":"Hello, everyone! I am long-time fan of Werewolf the Apolcaypse (my favorite White Wolf game line), but given I am from Brasil, it occurred to me I don't know a lot about how the rest of the world plays Werewolf the Apocalypse, and what they love and hate about the game line!<br /> <br /> My question right now, however, is pretty simple:<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Which are your Top 5 Favorite Tribes and Why?&quot;</span></i><br /> <br /> <b>BONUS:</b> Which is your Least Favorite Tribe and Why?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T23:57:26-08:00","id":811006,"title":"","content":"Top 5:<br /> 1. Red talons - heart of Garou nation. I love revised tribebook. It's one of my most favourite White Wolf book. Red talons view is very mature for me. Their look on Weaver, human herd ... theme of extinction and survival. I love the tribe for howling gifts, For everything<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 2. Shadow lords - slavic tribe, sneaky and cunning. I love lords politics, struggle for domination, being top of the tops, their history with Vampires, Camazots and being badfellows on Wild West. They have Bringers of the light - my favourite camp. I realy like Margrave, and Gutierez for redemptioning part of the bat. And for Gevudan story.<br /> 3. Get of Fenrir - I like them for scandinavian viking stories, for being not exactly stupid brutes. They have very fine tribe heroes, stories and legends. I like that they use hammers rather than klaives (made session around that theme), I like their courage and bravery and of course inner tribal politics. And their females are sexy<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> 4. Silver Fangs - three words - King Jonas Albrecht. I was'am'will be amazed by this character. I like fangs not for their madness but for their sane heroes like Grimfang, Albrecht, Loba and more. I like theme of fallen alphas, for shady camps like Grey raptors and I love when my player character frenzy everytime when someone speak about tribe weakness.<br /> 5. Glass walkers - I like them for they weaver affinity. They are much more complex for me after reading Book of the weaver. They are tech tribe in almost every aspect, physical and spiritual. But I like them for cutting edge tech, corporate wars with Pentex, DNA and Vampires, for things they do and for camps. I like concept of Cyberdogs and many many more.<br /> <br /> Honorable place: Black Spiral Dancers - evil mo.....rs. Tribe give's me plenty of ideas and oportunieties to scare, harass, annoy and outsmart my players. New gifts made them very terrifing (Grave claws!) besides new concept of Dancers who think that they already won is striking. And Dayalond<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Least Favourite tribe - there's no least favouirite.<br /> I love them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 01-18-2016, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T02:03:28-08:00","id":811041,"title":"","content":"Top 5?<br /> <br /> 1) Bone Gnawers. First there's the fun of playing the under dogs. Second the Gnawers, for me, have the best that the Children of Gaia and the Glass Walkers, but aren't saddled with the baggage those Tribes have. The ways they eschew both mainstream Garou culture, and how they interact with human issues are both fun and actually pragmatic. They can be just at home in a major metropolis as they can in a backwoods town of a couple families. They understand the need to do more than kill their way through problems, and how much work needs to be done to help reduce the massive human suffering coming from the poor and out castes of humanity to actually fight back against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> 2) Uktena (ok.... might be a bit of a theme here in terms of preferences..). By W20, they've been written very well as probably the best example of a Tribe with strong links to a select group of human cultures, without getting hung up on that origin. They might be strongest among Native American Tribes, but they've recognized the need to be more than that as an identity (unlike the Wendigo). The curiosity and mysticism angles are also a big plus for me. They're a Tribe that's about making characters that go out and do more than kill enemies, or getting caught up in one particular niche of what to go out and do.<br /> <br /> 3) Shadow Lords. A bit of a departure from the last two for sure. I just can't help but have a place in my heart for Tribe Manipulative Bastard. As is probably noticeable in my choices, I like Tribes that aren't too hung up on their human roots. They might know where they originated, but that's a minor concern for them compared to other things. I also love how they twist lupine hierarchy with human secret society methods to create a very unique culture to the Tribe alone.<br /> <br /> 4) Black Furies. The &quot;all female except for Metis&quot; part definitely knocks them down a lot for me, but I love them for playing a more traditional Garou Tribe. Without the big cause attached, they'd probably be #2 instead, but as is they beat out Tribes like the Fianna or Fenrir by having a much more balanced approach to things outside of gender politics.<br /> <br /> 5) Silver Fangs. Well... if I'm not going to play one of the Tribes more associated with the downtrodden/oppressed, I'm all in on the other direction of playing the elites. Much like the Gnawers, I definitely have a thing for them because of their strong value on not getting tied down to one area of the world or one ethnic group. I'm very glad for Revised giving a completely different spin on their weakness, even if W20 seems to be going back a bit on that. They're also good for my clear love of Tribes that have a tendency to buck tradition, but from the position of power instead.<br /> <br /> Least favorite:<br /> <br /> Easy. As I've probably spent too much time on before, the Red Talons are absolutely the bottom for me.<br /> <br /> Even the solid writing of some of their material can't save them from a fundamental flaw: they're only real thing is being more wolf than you. There's no real complexity in their rejection of humanity, there's no cost like the Glass Walkers suffer for being disconnected from the wolf, or things to really explore in role-play. I have never seen (including threads here about this) anything about them that I don't like better as just playing a lupus - or member of a lupus only/dominated camp, including inter-Tribal camps - of another Tribe. Their philosophy is also so backwards, it basically says that a non-homid Tribe is either controlled entirely by insane or stupid Garou. The never ending need to prove themselves the wolfiest wolves that ever wolfed is actually a completely human way of thinking. Wolves don't care about controlling other species, or if other species go extinct. Nature is brutal, and it doesn't need them to be brutal for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T05:21:24-08:00","id":811069,"title":"","content":"Glass Walkers, Shadow Lords, Uktena, Fianna and Bone Gnawers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T10:39:40-08:00","id":811206,"title":"","content":"1- Bone gnawers. If they could have pure breed, they'd be the undisputed masters of the garou nation. But the most important thing is that I really, Really dig the punk-magic hobo. <br /> <br /> 2 Get of fenrir. The closest tribe to gaia's original intentions for the garou (warriors) . I love their meritocratic 'Get good or don't join' mentality. Merely surviving the rites of passage makes you a badass. That, and their totem was a garou who became an Incarnae. Yep. <br /> <br /> 3- Glass walkers. Merely for the faction that becomes a load of terminators. <br /> <br /> 4/5 uktena/Fianna. They have cool things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:22:03-08:00","id":811255,"title":"","content":"Get of Fenris- I REALLY didn't like this tribe at first, seeing them as nothing more than brutes. But as I read the revised tribebook, I started to understand how they work, and I liked it. The idea that each and every Fenrir has to prove themselves, regardless of breeding or breed, is neat. That, and how much they base their culture on controlling their Rage instead of letting it control them, makes for interesting playing.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords- As with the Fenrir, the Lords base more emphasis on skill versus breeding makes these guys interesting. That, and the fact that they are aware of the wrongs they did and are trying to fix them.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers- City wolves without losing their wolf edge, pretty much. I also like the idea that they choose to be on the streets and do their good there. That, and that they are democratic.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs- As hidebound as they are, I do like the structure of the tribe. These guys are kings of the yesteryear, wanting to hold onto their old ways no matter what. I like the idea of this tribe struggling in the modern world, and failing.<br /> <br /> <i>-The not so favorite</i><br /> <br /> Fianna- Aside from their metis hate, I generally am sad that no one plays the Fianna's other flaws. These guys are the strongest supporters of the Silver Fangs, and as such, tend to believe the old stories of War of Rage.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia- These guys are more here, because they've never really gotten a fair shake. As such, there are a variety of ways to do them 'right'. All better than the tribebooks they've gotten.<br /> <br /> Uktena&amp;Wendigo- These are here not because I have an issue with them. But rather because I will never play them due to me being Finnish and far from America. Maybe someday sami-wendigo, but we'll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T12:22:06-08:00","id":811256,"title":"","content":"I think pretty much everyone likes the Bone Gnawers. They have a bit of a sense of humor, the underdog status (no pun intended) and the low-urban magic is unique and fun. I'd say they are one of my favorite tribes. The Children of Gaia can be great under the right portrayal and I think they get a bad rep.<br /> <br /> While the revised tribebook made me like them more, the Stargazers didn't quite click with me. I don't hate or dislike them, it just didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:02:28-08:00","id":811278,"title":"","content":"Silver Fangs. The blood of alpha wolves and kings of men flows through their veins. Each of Falcon's chosen has been called, not necessarily as a leader, but to be an example, a paragon that the rest of the Garou Nation can depend upon. But creeping madness infects their souls, tainting their honorable intentions and noble goals. How can the Silver Fangs save the world when they can not save themselves?<br /> <br /> Uktena. Black secrets and a history marred by war, but not bitterness. The Uktena have shown wisdom and adaptability following the Westward Expansion, but their mystery engenders mistrust among the other tribes, and that may be their eventual downfall. The road to perdition is paved with the best of intentions. <br /> <br /> Red Talons. To those with wolf-minds, millions of years is not so different from yesterday. The young of Griffin remember when great beasts walked Gaia, and they remind the other Garou that it was not so long ago in the reckoning of the Mother. Since the humans escaped the just culling of the Impergium, they have driven the world toward annihilation, a walking, consuming, breeding extinction event. Blood calls for blood. One species going extinct to save all the rest... it is but a small price to pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:27:21-08:00","id":811293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=811255#post811255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uktena&amp;Wendigo- These are here not because I have an issue with them. But rather because I will never play them due to me being Finnish and far from America. Maybe someday sami-wendigo, but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Uktena have gotten increasingly more like the Gnawers and Children of Gaia in being were oppressed people are. It's really easy to have Uktena almost anywhere these days because of it.<br /> <br /> Also, if you are following the BNS material for the new MET Werewolf book, it is taking this a bit further. In MET canon, Sami Wendigo are officially a thing (basically the metaplot for MET has caused all the old Wendigo bloodlines among the Eurasian indigenous arctic peoples from before the Tribe crossed into North America to reawaken; leading to a massive divide in the Tribe between those that have become consumed by their identity as the &quot;angry Native American&quot; Tribe, and those that want to move towards a bigger tent Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T21:17:56-08:00","id":811533,"title":"","content":"1.) Stargazers: I loved their take of buddhism and merging it with their views of Gaian cosmology<br /> 2.) Silent Strider: Egyptian fluff. Tragic flaw. all around badasses<br /> 3.) Shadow Lords: My most common played tribe. Cunning, ruthless, understands the sense of doing wrong to defeat an opponent for the greater good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T03:48:01-08:00","id":811653,"title":"","content":"My top five favorites...<br /> <br /> 1. Glass Walkers, especially when I use my homebrewed Roman origins and motifs for them. But even played 100% canon, they're still my favorite tribe<br /> 2. Get of Fenris, because Vikings are awesome<br /> 3. Black Furies, I like both Ancient Greece and the Woman Warrior archetype, so they are a choice tribe for me!<br /> 4. Stargazers, love the Eastern mystic angle they have. I hate that Revised Edition had them leave the Garou Nation, so I ignore that part and keep them in<br /> 5. Uktena, once again, I like the mysticism and the fact that they have Native American origins but aren't hung up on it like the Wendigo<br /> <br /> My least favorite tribe is the Red Talons, hands down. They are such a shallow tribe in my opinion and unlike the other tribes, you can't really add your own depth to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 01-19-2016, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:11:04-08:00","id":811771,"title":"","content":"Bone Gnawers - Because there the only ones that really &quot;get it.&quot;<br /> Glass Walkers - I love the idea of a street werewolf with cybernetic implants.<br /> Get of Fenris - Viking barbarian werewolves are awesome.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I like every tribe in WtA for various reasons. In that, there is not a single tribe that I wouldn't play in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:11:53-08:00","id":811810,"title":"","content":"Top 5 tribes:<br /> 1. Uktena- the mixture of mysticism and brawn makes for an interesting character. The idea that this tribe will go to great lengths to uncover or recover hidden secrets is great for both short and long term goals as a player or storyteller.<br /> 2. Red Talons- I like the feel of desperation, the long hard struggle that the Talons and Griffon fight. I do have issues with the tribe being murder hobos and generally play one that is desperately trying to understand why humanity is so destructive.<br /> 3. Silver Fangs- I like the gifts, sue me.<br /> 4. Bone Gnawers- while I dislike certain aspects the Gnawers are fun to play it is always best to be overlooked.<br /> 5. White Howlers- this tribe has fascinated me since I first picked up Werewolf the Apocalypse in any historical game the White Howlers will be my first choice.<br /> Tribes I dislike:<br /> 1. Stargazers-feels like they don't fit. <br /> 2. Glass Walkers-nice concept, just doesn't appeal to me.<br /> 3. Fianna- nothing more than not my thing. <br /> 4. Black Furies- really not my cup of tea, the Talons get slammed regularly for blaming the species of humans for the wrongs of the world but the Furies at least as written do the same but blame gender.<br /> 5. Shadow Lords- I don't like mind games.<br /> <br /> The tribe I hate and would prefer falling to the Wyrm instead of the Howlers: The Children of Gaia. This tribe as written across all editions rank as the Yuppie poster child of white guilt. The concept is neat the execution reads like a whine fest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:13:49-08:00","id":811857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=811810#post811810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Red Talons- I like the feel of desperation, the long hard struggle that the Talons and Griffon fight. I do have issues with the tribe being murder hobos and generally play one that is desperately trying to understand why humanity is so destructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think the murder hobo problem, and general issue with the tribe, stems from two sources; The players of Talons going for the most polarizing version of the tribe. And fellow players not bothering to understand how a lupus acts. I've seen this with some lupus played in general. Then again, sometimes lupus players DO overdo it.<br /> <br /> I think a great Red Talon concept would be a mediator whose player gives enough clues to other players to know what the character means. So that players who are not interested in wolf behaviour can still figure them out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=811810#post811810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tribe I hate and would prefer falling to the Wyrm instead of the Howlers: The Children of Gaia. This tribe as written across all editions rank as the Yuppie poster child of white guilt. The concept is neat the execution reads like a whine fest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept would be great, but sadly, no one has ever actually done anything with it. Also, the problem is as much that CoGies tend to be, well, mostly white, despite being a cosmopolitan tribe.<br /> <br /> The saddest part about them is, that there are plenty of examples for a less than cuddly healer/peacemaker. Mary Seacole was known for both her shrewd business sense and her mission to care for wounded soldiers during the Crimean war, as an example. War medics, relief workers, search and rescue workers, etc. Why is it so hard to use these and the cultural heritage of the middle east (sciences, medicine,etc.) to make the tribe interesting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=811293#post811293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Uktena have gotten increasingly more like the Gnawers and Children of Gaia in being were oppressed people are. It's really easy to have Uktena almost anywhere these days because of it.<br /> <br /> Also, if you are following the BNS material for the new MET Werewolf book, it is taking this a bit further. In MET canon, Sami Wendigo are officially a thing (basically the metaplot for MET has caused all the old Wendigo bloodlines among the Eurasian indigenous arctic peoples from before the Tribe crossed into North America to reawaken; leading to a massive divide in the Tribe between those that have become consumed by their identity as the &quot;angry Native American&quot; Tribe, and those that want to move towards a bigger tent Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I just don't think Sami Wendigo are really okay yet. I do think the tribe needs changing, but it would be good if it came from other sources than just adding more nations to the mix.<br /> <br /> As for Uktena, while they are cosmopolitan, their basic structure is still very Native American.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T23:12:19-08:00","id":812405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=811653#post811653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My top five favorites...<br /> <br /> 1. Glass Walkers, especially when I use my homebrewed Roman origins and motifs for them. But even played 100% canon, they're still my favorite tribe<br /> 2. Get of Fenris, because Vikings are awesome</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Fenrir are anti-Vikings who hold the Aesir to be their enemies. Mention that you're, say, asatru around one of them, and there's a good chance that you end up on the ass-end of an asskicking, at best. Revised deconstructed them and then built them up anew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T02:09:00-08:00","id":812457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812405#post812405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the Fenrir are anti-Vikings who hold the Aesir to be their enemies. Mention that you're, say, asatru around one of them, and there's a good chance that you end up on the ass-end of an asskicking, at best. Revised deconstructed them and then built them up anew.</div> </div> </div> </div>I play 1e, not Revised. Besides, I use Rule Zero a lot in my games. Stargazers are still in the Garou Nation and the Glass Walkers are heavily tied to Ancient Rome in my games (with their founder being the She-Wolf who fed Romulus and Remus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T03:10:25-08:00","id":812476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812457#post812457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I play 1e, not Revised. Besides, I use Rule Zero a lot in my games. Stargazers are still in the Garou Nation and the Glass Walkers are heavily tied to Ancient Rome in my games (with their founder being the She-Wolf who fed Romulus and Remus).</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. And how do you cope with them following the bringer of Ragnarok and devourer of all good vikings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:29:32-08:00","id":812509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812476#post812476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay. And how do you cope with them following the bringer of Ragnarok and devourer of all good vikings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Never really thought of that, I'm more familiar with Classical Mythology than Norse, so you do have a fair point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:38:50-08:00","id":812519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812509#post812509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never really thought of that, I'm more familiar with Classical Mythology than Norse, so you do have a fair point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest you do. In general, every mythology in the world is a primo resource for actually playing and running Werewolf.<br /> <br /> What Revised did with them is quite a bit more reasonable then what they were originaly presented as.<br /> For reference in more common terms: 1st edition claims that Christians follow The Beast. That's how absurd it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 01-20-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T05:47:59-08:00","id":812526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812519#post812519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suggest you do. In general, every mythology in the world is a primo resource for actually playing and running Werewolf.<br /> <br /> What Revised did with them is quite a bit more reasonable then what they were originaly presented as.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I will do some more research on Norse Mythology (and maybe some other mythologies too).<br /> <br /> I never really liked Revised because the metaplot became too overbearing and overtly grimdark. In my opinion, Revised stopped being a World of Darkness and became a World of Pitch Blackness, so I stick to 1e/2e and the X20 books. Again, this is just my opinion, so take my words with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> That being said, I did like one thing Revised did with the Get of Fenris, and that was removing all that Nazi bullshit from the earlier editions. The Swords of Heimdall are the one group that the Revised Editions got rid of that I am actually glad are gone. And in my metaplot-free games, they never existed in the first place.<br /> <br /> And yes, I will admit, there were some things in 1e and 2e that were silly, I will admit, like the whole Beast thing you mentioned. I just think Revised sort of swung too hard in the other direction and over-corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 01-20-2016, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T07:28:11-08:00","id":812586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812526#post812526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, I will do some more research on Norse Mythology (and maybe some other mythologies too).<br /> <br /> I never really liked Revised because the metaplot became too overbearing and overtly grimdark. In my opinion, Revised stopped being a World of Darkness and became a World of Pitch Blackness, so I stick to 1e/2e and the X20 books. Again, this is just my opinion, so take my words with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> That being said, I did like one thing Revised did with the Get of Fenris, and that was removing all that Nazi bullshit from the earlier editions. The Swords of Heimdall are the one group that the Revised Editions got rid of that I am actually glad are gone. And in my metaplot-free games, they never existed in the first place.<br /> <br /> And yes, I will admit, there were some things in 1e and 2e that were silly, I will admit, like the whole Beast thing you mentioned. I just think Revised sort of swung too hard in the other direction and over-corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never saw the metaplot as particularly constraining for Werewolf. That may be on account of hanging around the forums to hear Ethan Skemp mention that he didn't want to really take away anything from any given group, so that was why parties like Black Tooth's killer or the pack that raised the Perfect Metis in time for Apocalypse are never named. Even without that statement, though, most of the material was a super-light touch compared to, say, Vampire. The Stargazers might have packed up officially, but they certainly weren't near-completely exterminated, like the Ravnos, and there was still material assuming that you might actually play one or two or more that stayed behind. It was so light that most people don't even remember the &quot;Garou and Fera stop being born for the end, every new birth is Kinfolk instead&quot; part; you'd have to talk about that in things like the new MET Werewolf that BNS is making, and from what I can figure, they didn't feel the need to mention it at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:59:50-08:00","id":812692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812526#post812526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That being said, I did like one thing Revised did with the Get of Fenris, and that was removing all that Nazi bullshit from the earlier editions. The Swords of Heimdall are the one group that the Revised Editions got rid of that I am actually glad are gone. And in my metaplot-free games, they never existed in the first place.<br /> <br /> And yes, I will admit, there were some things in 1e and 2e that were silly, I will admit, like the whole Beast thing you mentioned. I just think Revised sort of swung too hard in the other direction and over-corrected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, the revised tribebooks (minus a few) were a lot more considerate and better reseatched on how the tribes would be, coming from the areas they did. Silent Strider and Fenrir books are one of the best, simply because they portray a very complex image of the tribes, with faults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812586#post812586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was so light that most people don't even remember the &quot;Garou and Fera stop being born for the end, every new birth is Kinfolk instead&quot; part; you'd have to talk about that in things like the new MET Werewolf that BNS is making, and from what I can figure, they didn't feel the need to mention it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard a lot of stories where that change came from, but it always seemed a rather limiting thing. I do think most people just out and out ignored it, because it didn't fit WtA well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:54:46-08:00","id":812767,"title":"","content":"I'm actually unsure what my top 5 favorite tribes are, though I'm pretty sure glasswalkers and get of fenris are up there, I just can't decide on the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812405#post812405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the ass-end of an asskicking, at best.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will of course be adding the phrase &quot;the ass-end of an asskicking&quot; to my personal lexicon now. I expect it to come up decently often, particularly when playing smash 4<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1069-archmage-joda","name":"Archmage Joda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:03:52-08:00","id":812824,"title":"","content":"On the BNS and the reduction in Changers being born: the gamma slice does actually mention it, and it being reversed. Whatever big war happened (that wasn't fleshed out in the gamma slice) did massive damage to the Garou populations, but the aftermath somehow also lead to their bloodlines breeding far stronger than before the big war (they might explain this in more detail, or leave it vague, it's hard to say). That's why there are things in the upcoming book like the ancient Eurasian Wendigo bloodlines suddenly producing kin and Garou again.<br /> <br /> Seems a pretty simple way of dealing with it that doesn't involved a retcon, or just ignoring it. Part of the spiritual aftermath of the big war caused by the appearance of the Red Eye was to reverse the trend of the Fera dying out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:33:58-08:00","id":813070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812824#post812824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the BNS and the reduction in Changers being born: the gamma slice does actually mention it, and it being reversed. Whatever big war happened (that wasn't fleshed out in the gamma slice) did massive damage to the Garou populations, but the aftermath somehow also lead to their bloodlines breeding far stronger than before the big war (they might explain this in more detail, or leave it vague, it's hard to say). That's why there are things in the upcoming book like the ancient Eurasian Wendigo bloodlines suddenly producing kin and Garou again.<br /> <br /> Seems a pretty simple way of dealing with it that doesn't involved a retcon, or just ignoring it. Part of the spiritual aftermath of the big war caused by the appearance of the Red Eye was to reverse the trend of the Fera dying out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I'd rather have a retcon to fit in the material that they did, really..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:06:39-08:00","id":813119,"title":"","content":"Hard to say but would have to say.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords Because I go for hard edged &quot;For the greater good&quot; Ruthlessness<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs because I like to play insufferable entitled assholes.<br /> <br /> Redtalons I like for their Human hate<br /> <br /> My last pick... varys... on any givewn day between fianna, for their nobility, and connections with the fae, and either the stargazes or uketena for their mysticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T00:59:23-08:00","id":813232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812586#post812586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never saw the metaplot as particularly constraining for Werewolf. That may be on account of hanging around the forums to hear Ethan Skemp mention that he didn't want to really take away anything from any given group, so that was why parties like Black Tooth's killer or the pack that raised the Perfect Metis in time for Apocalypse are never named. Even without that statement, though, most of the material was a super-light touch compared to, say, Vampire. The Stargazers might have packed up officially, but they certainly weren't near-completely exterminated, like the Ravnos, and there was still material assuming that you might actually play one or two or more that stayed behind. It was so light that most people don't even remember the &quot;Garou and Fera stop being born for the end, every new birth is Kinfolk instead&quot; part; you'd have to talk about that in things like the new MET Werewolf that BNS is making, and from what I can figure, they didn't feel the need to mention it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something that I've always found funny. People tend to treat metaplot as a very universal thing in WoD, and it's not. Very little of the metaplot actually happens or is particularly important to Werewolf. It was Vampire and Mage who were subservient to the concept. In general I really appreciated how optional everything was and how little reference there was for the 2-3 big plot books for Werewolf. It was there if you wanted it, but no one was going to hammer you over the head about it. I think it really is about Ethan Skemp being a very good hand at what he was doing and trying to keep the experience as open ended as possible. Then again, Werewolf tends to be the most misunderstood game among people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T04:49:01-08:00","id":813285,"title":"","content":"I dig the whole &quot;hippy&quot; thing the Children of Gaia got going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:02:19-08:00","id":813345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=813232#post813232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something that I've always found funny. People tend to treat metaplot as a very universal thing in WoD, and it's not. Very little of the metaplot actually happens or is particularly important to Werewolf. It was Vampire and Mage who were subservient to the concept. In general I really appreciated how optional everything was and how little reference there was for the 2-3 big plot books for Werewolf. It was there if you wanted it, but no one was going to hammer you over the head about it. I think it really is about Ethan Skemp being a very good hand at what he was doing and trying to keep the experience as open ended as possible. <b>Then again, Werewolf tends to be the most misunderstood game among people.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. Hunter and Changeling are typically targets of pronounced, non-sensical aggression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:36:49-08:00","id":813360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=813345#post813345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about that. Hunter and Changeling are typically targets of pronounced, non-sensical aggression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think Werewolf is misunderstood by those who aren't as lore savvy as we. We've seen plenty of &quot;Garou are xenophobic racists&quot; and such here sometimes.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Changeling and Hunter are generally more misunderstood. Poor Changeling to the point where the good stuff is overshadowed by some of the art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T03:28:26-08:00","id":814751,"title":"","content":"My old comment is now different , thanks to years of play I think I love every tribe.<br /> It's always really difficult for me to chose a tribe now, when it's time to play.<br /> <br /> My favorite tribe are the Red Talons.<br /> I think it's the deeper tribe, savages and pures, close to Gaia and to primal animism. <br /> They gave me the deepest adventures I ever played at the table with my friends.<br /> <br /> I have a special relationship with the Silver Fangs, as one of my main characters, is one of them.<br /> <br /> I dislike no tribe. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 05-10-2019, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T07:35:24-08:00","id":814835,"title":"","content":"1: Shadow Lords<br /> This tribe has done a stand up job of being the ones to do the things the kings cant be seen doing for the Nation. Their codes and ethos can hold and call for a lot of diversity in service to gaia from the shadows. Their hearts like rolling Thunder and their vengeance like lightning cleaving through the sky and their patience and moments of cunning as eerie as the calm after the storm.<br /> <br /> 2: Children of Gaia<br /> I really enjoy how well this tribe has endured with their peaceful, merciful, pure Totem of Unicorn in a society of psychopaths. <br /> Because they are just as strong, just as devoted and just as badass if you get on the wrong side of them. Sure they get played as hippys and naieve dogooders a lot. But for every one of them theres a non-apologist doing or sacrificing what needs to be done in Gaias name.<br /> Plus I really like how they've identified one head of the Wyrm as theIr anti, their direct opposition of all they hold dear and fight against in thought, concept and physically.<br /> <br /> 3: Black Furies<br /> There's a beautiful elegance to this Tribe. As dangerous as they are their mysyicism and long established lines of spuritual broods under Pegasus and the traditions and ties they've woven make them as unique as they are ferocious. Strong females one and all. I dig all of this.<br /> <br /> 4: Red Talons<br /> Primal doesnt mean stupid. Instinctual doesnt mean ignorant. This Tribe has a heavy focus on the insight that comes from a different perspective. They get used a bit for pvp and derailing of stories by some in a side quest to confront humanity but when you cut to the core of them theres a reflection of loss and lines of extinction that's very real and demands a foot (or paw) be put down and say &quot;enough is enough.&quot; <br /> <br /> 5: Silver Fangs<br /> They get a lot of hate, but they take it in their stride. They get a lot of the blame, but they continue to make those difficult decisions no one else really wants to make or be held accountable for. They have a rich and incredible infrastructure that although seen as dated by most they still continue to honor those that came before them and uphold old deals and bargains made centuries before. I really like that they take their role seriously and honor it as much as themselves while taking the slings and arrows of all around them. Noblility. I really them.<br /> <br /> I dont really dislike any of the Tribes, they all have their pros and cons and I accept them as they are. Imperfections and all, especially for the imperfections, because being perfect and always right would be boring. To me anyway. The world is dying, the Apocalypse is coming (or already has), when will you Rage and why and what for? You're happy to die but what are you willing to live for? Now fight for it.<br /> <br /> But you asked, so I guess the tribes I would least favor to play would be...<br /> <br /> 1: Stargazers<br /> I love the introspective and insight. But these guys seems to unattached to the realitys the Garou face. Kalindo looks cool, but I dont think it really is. I think removing them from the Nation and heading to the beast courts was the right move for them.<br /> <br /> 2. Bonegnawers<br /> I love the whole hobo thing and the urban outcasts living on the fringes of society and surviving in poverty as the underdogs. But really, personal survival over sacrifice and duty isnt my bag. Sure they snub their snouts at everything, but it seems more like they do it because they lost it. Not because they didnt need it (pure breed, strict adherence to the litany, ancestors etc). If you cant respect yourself yada yada...<br /> <br /> 3: Fianna<br /> I think I'm just maybe a little tired of the whole &quot;we're drunk and all Galliards&quot; direction I've seen from day one. Plus, I dont like Changeling which for some reason they are heavily into and occasionally put more emphasis on than other things more common to the nation. Although they do have some interesting camps and I do like the proposed extreme emotional states.<br /> <br /> 5: Bunyip<br /> I still like them more than the Nuwisha and wonder if maybe they should have been the Tribe (breed) that left the world in exodus on Dream and Spirit Quests and have maybe made a return with all they have learned and found out there as the apocalypse draws nearer with Gateways and Pathways for all to follow and see for themselves. But I think it's also fitting theres a tribe that was wiped out by the garou themselves with no good coming from it. So maybe its appropriate they are here on my list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:41:12-08:00","id":819183,"title":"","content":"Hahaha!<br /> <br /> Wow! So much good stuff on this poll!<br /> <br /> First off, thanks for the input! I was highly curious before, and I was surprised at some of these results! For the curious, the poll so far is:<br /> <br /> 1. Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords (9/0)<br /> 2. Get of Fenris (7/0)<br /> 3. Bone Gnawers (7/1)<br /> 4. Uktena and Red Talons (6/1)<br /> 5. Glass Walker and Black Furies (5/0)<br /> 6. Silent Striders (2/0)<br /> 7. Fianna and Stargazers (3/2)<br /> 8. Wendigo (1/1)<br /> 9. Children of Gaia (2/3)<br /> <br /> <br /> The numbers at the left are Favorite votes, while the ones on the right are the Least Favorite votes!<br /> <br /> Very surprised at how loved the Silver Fangs, Red Talons and Uktena are, and how many negative votes Fianna and Children got! Also, I was expecting a bigger Get and Bone Gnawer turnout! Interesting stuff! Keep voting, oh my peeps from Werewolf fandom!<br /> <br /> My own votes are:<br /> <br /> 1. Get of Fenris: Absolutely love them. I like their stance on strength, and the meritocracy inside the Tribe, just as I like their hipocrisy in how some Get abuse those rules to bully and abuse the weak. I like flawed Tribes because they give the player an opportunity to shine. Furthermore, their view of the viking legends being completely bogus is highly attractive (although I feel that, if such was the case, they could have gone way deeper into that subject) and their roots on Germany, and the Third Reich, are also awesome plot fodder. Also, vikings. Cuz vikingz. And hot valkyries.<br /> <br /> 2. Silver Fangs: The first Tribe I played for the reasons most people probably did; they had white fur, were the heroes of legend and that was enough at the time. I do love their roots in Russia, the aspect of aging, crazy leadership that young pups have to somehow deal with WITHOUT forgetting they ARE Silver Fangs. One of my main gripes with the Tribe is Albrecht who goes all 'I don't care, bro' about his Tribe's customs, where I feel a good Silver Fang player would have worked within the system to try and heal her Tribe. Also, Clan Crescent Moon is the best.<br /> <br /> 3. Shadow Lords: The dark knights of the werewolves, the guys who will do what others won't. Their homeland is riddled with great plot hooks with Kupala, the Tzimisce, the mortal systems of oppression and violence, and if you don't like that? Their Camps and outlook are some of the most unique amongst the Tribes.<br /> <br /> 4. Black Furies: I love the idea of the Furies. They have a strong theme of Feminility and Motherhood, they have a kickass homeland and aesthetics. I love the idea they can embrace what it means to be Female, in all aspects, without sounding like angry, privileged bloggers. Their understanding of the struggles of women all around the globe comes from a deeply spiritual place, and their connection to mysticism and the Wyld is just icing on the cake. Also, great Camps.<br /> <br /> 5. Silent Striders: Why u no love the Striders, forum?! Come on, now! They have an amazing, and unique, perpective of what it is to be a werewolf without a home, without territory. Their goals are clear, their station unique, even their forms are unique-looking. They hail from Old Egypt, they are the sworn enemies of one of the best Vampire Clans and if that was not enough, they also have their whole drama with their ancestors. Great Tribe for players everywhere!<br /> <br /> Least Favorite: Stargazers<br /> <br /> They just don't fit. I like their idea, but they are too different. They fit with the Hengeyokai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>IA","edited":{"userid":462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","user":"Tchokes","date":". 01-29-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/462-tchokes","name":"Tchokes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:06:27-08:00","id":826706,"title":"","content":"I'm not a big werewolf fan, but I have my own rating.<br /> <br /> 0. Fera, especially the Eastern Ones (Hengeyokai). I like Kitsune and Nuwisha for their cunning and sociality, and adore the whole Mokole idea for were-(Jesus!)-dragons!<br /> <br /> 1. Glass Wolkers. The Technocrats of the WtA. They look cool and very stylish. I think I like them so much because the tribe differs from the rest in so many ways. They are, howdoyousayit... remarkable!<br /> <br /> 2. Get of Fenris. Their viking style makes them the ultimate badasses in the finest sense of the word. The werewolf's brutality suits them very well.<br /> <br /> 3. Stargazers. For that eastern air of tranquility and mastery of Rage. Shaolin monks with claws and frenzy - sounds awesome.<br /> <br /> 4/5. Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords. For those slavic fables and air of superiority. And maybe Fianna - I like Celts, just that simple.<br /> <br /> For the least favorite tribe... I can name Red Talons. I just can't get their anti-human ideas. Too odd for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T08:47:14-08:00","id":829752,"title":"","content":"Interesting question, and interesting answers. I'll give my two cents, though I'm not from the cut the OP asked (I'm also from Brasil).<br /> <br /> 0 - First I should point that I'm also a fan of other Fera, though not so much of the Emerald Court (not so much into the Kung Fu Land of WW). The strange Ananasi are the first to me, but there are few if any Fera I don't like.<br /> <br /> 1 - Children of Gaia: The only thing I hate about them is the poor treatment they received from game development. The idea of a beast of Rage and Righteous Fury holding to humanistic ideals is very appealing to me. It is a hard tribe to play, and it doesn't have all that canon material to really support it. Instead, you have CoG Revised... but the core principle and all the possibilities... I simply can't not love the Children of Gaia.<br /> <br /> 2 - Black Furies: Greek warrior-women with mysticism and discussions about gender, and space to work all of those questions in the way and dept you wish. I simply love them. You can be a mother, a damsel, a witch, a bloody murderer, a humanist, a misandric bitch, or simply be whatever you could be in any other tribe. You can raise the questions of gender with the most simple roles, because you're a woman not doing a woman's job, or you can throw all the questions, because your tribe justifies whatever you want to be. There are so much you can do with them, that it is a shame that so many players only see the misandric warrior-bitches.<br /> <br /> 3 - Glass Walkers: A tribe that evolved? Who wouldn't like it? It is complex, but all tribes are. What most get my attention on the tribe is the idea that you don't have to be a tree-hugger to be in the service of Earth. And that you can change, progress, evolve.<br /> <br /> 4 - Uktena: It doesn't seem to me as much a cultural stereotype as most tribes are, specially a non-european tribe. Of course, they do have theirs. But at least you can graduate without the canon setting saying that you are a traitor to your culture.<br /> <br /> 5 - Stargazers: Hard to say what I really think of this tribe. A part of me want to cast them as one of the worst. But I simply can't. The biggest problem of the Stargazers is their relationship with the East, in the sense that they are THE Eastern tribe, being mostly defined simply by being from the East, and the East being defined by being their homeland. But if you take this aside, them the themes and interests of the Stargazers <u>are</u> interesting. Maybe, though, they could work better as a camp of the Children of Gaia...<br /> <br /> This list was awfully hard to create. I'm not so sure about the rankings, and I'm in doubt about other tribes that I think deserved attention. The Shadowlords, the ones who do what have to be done even if this means they will be hated by their peers. The Silent Striders with their link to the Dark Umbra, the ghosts of humanity, and ancient grudges with the Followers of Set (my best vampire PC was Kin to the Silent Striders when alive, and she is deeply interested in the current station of the tribe. She is a loyal Kin, even in death and knowing they will hunt her). For most of my life as a player I loved above all the Bone Gnawers, the underdogs that do the work of Gaia even being poorly treated and almost never recognized by their efforts. Silver Fangs, Get of Fenris and Fianna are very interesting tribes from more than one aspect.<br /> <br /> My most hated tribe, though, is the Red Talons. I don't get very well with the Wendigo, either (their hate of the white-people takes too much from what could be a great tribe), but the Talons are over the top. <b>Heavy Arms</b> already surmised very well their failings. They're not a bad idea, by themselves. But they're an idea best handled as a camp of any other tribe. They have no culture of their own except for being wolves, and wolves have no culture in the way we talk about when talking about tribes (wolves do have non-innate behaviors that should be called cultural by scientific standards, but this goes beyond the scope of this discussion for me). A lupus is already an option in any tribe, and hating humanity is already an option for <u>any</u> character, even homids. By the way, given that the game implies the shapeshifters being older than humanity, but <b>never gave any hint to how they shifted into something not human</b>, all the stances in with the Fera claim to be completely separated from humanity seem completely silly to me. It is an option for a character, of course, and even a camp, but an entire tribe? Not. Not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T17:51:54-08:00","id":829936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=829752#post829752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> By the way, given that the game implies the shapeshifters being older than humanity, but <b>never gave any hint to how they shifted into something not human</b>, all the stances in with the Fera claim to be completely separated from humanity seem completely silly to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragon Wars section of Shattered Dreams actually covers that. The Mokole Breedbook also presented the place that Homid form occupies as a niche that could be theoretically occupied by any being that's reasonably close to possessing the same traits that made the niche possible, and laid down that the Kings the Mokole speak of were just that type of being, so that's one example from back in 1999.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:52:08-08:00","id":830135,"title":"","content":"While it all depends on how they are portrayed in games, speaking my favorites.<br /> <br /> 1) Silver Fangs. To me the main appeal of werewolf is the whole Barbaric Society in modern times and nothing exemplifies that better than the Silver Fangs. However many DMs either play the bad of the tribe without the balancing good of it.<br /> <br /> 2) Shadowlords. Interesting gift and some nice concepts to play with.<br /> <br /> 3) Fenrir. Surprisingly good diplomatic gift-wise but aside from that i like them on concept even though very few players/dm portray them well.<br /> <br /> 4) Glasswalkers. Technogifts!<br /> <br /> 5) Child of Gaia. Well properly played they can be awesome when not.....CoG rev Tribebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> Least Favorites<br /> <br /> 1) Fianna. They are boring, the only niche they occupy that is not done better by other tribes is being drunk. Are they the warrior tribe? No, the fenrir are better at it. Are they the galliard tribe? No, Silver Fangs are better at it. Are they the &quot;human centric&quot; tribe? No, the Glass walkers are better at it. Are they the tribe that keeps the other happy and united? No, the Children of Gaia are better at it. So they are the Bro tribe.......yeah they are so necessary. <br /> <br /> 2) Wendigo. Too geographical dependent.<br /> <br /> 3) Stargazers. They dont fit with the rest in both setting and gameplay. And worse yet, while kalindo should be available to everyone is apparently only domain for them.<br /> <br /> 4) Silent Stridder. They seems a NPC only tribe. And it kinda forces the DM to know about wraith/ghosts.<br /> <br /> 5) Ronins. I hate the name and i hate how they are the DM hammer to force players to &quot;play the game&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-15-2016, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:16:03-08:00","id":830621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=829936#post829936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragon Wars section of Shattered Dreams actually covers that. The Mokole Breedbook also presented the place that Homid form occupies as a niche that could be theoretically occupied by any being that's reasonably close to possessing the same traits that made the niche possible, and laid down that the Kings the Mokole speak of were just that type of being, so that's one example from back in 1999.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know, though not surprising, given the sheer size of the written material of the game. But now I'm definitely curious about this.<br /> <br /> Even then, though, given how late it was presented and how, my arguments still apply good enough for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T21:08:40-08:00","id":830784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=830621#post830621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's good to know, though not surprising, given the sheer size of the written material of the game. But now I'm definitely curious about this.<br /> <br /> Even then, though, given how late it was presented and how, my arguments still apply good enough for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was originally presented in the book that made the biggest claims about it, nearly seventeen years ago. The player's guides that introduced the Mokole carried barely a hint of it; I was rather confused when I first read it, myself, because it was going kind of Chrono Trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T01:16:58-08:00","id":830892,"title":"","content":"I honestly have a hard time deciding on the favourite tribe. I think that the Silent Striders, Glass Walkers and Shadow Lords tie for the top, but I find all the Tribes intriguing and playable. Some of them do need more work then the others to work well, though, but I've never balked at doing some R&amp;D to make things click.<br /> <br /> I do believe, though that Bone Gnawers need to move away from the hobo shtick, that the Black Furies need to differentiate between feminism and misandry and not serve as a soapbox, and that the Children of Gaia need a serious examination as a concept of warriors looking for peace. So maybe I'd say that they are the three tribes I'm least likely to play without tinkering with them to make them more workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T23:47:24-08:00","id":836274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=812405#post812405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the Fenrir are anti-Vikings who hold the Aesir to be their enemies. Mention that you're, say, asatru around one of them, and there's a good chance that you end up on the ass-end of an asskicking, at best. Revised deconstructed them and then built them up anew.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call them &quot;anti-Vikings,&quot; since even the Revised book makes it clear that they were involved in Viking culture.<br /> <br /> While the Revised tribebook is one of my favorites, I feel like the entire spin of Odin the Enemy Vampire was an over-reaction to the Einherjar in Dark Ages Vampire.<br /> <br /> I had to take the whole thing with a grain of salt. While it makes sense to portray Odin as the adversary of Great Fenris, since they will kill each other at Ragnarok, the same speaker also lists Loki as one of Fenris\u2019 enemies, which as far as I know is not consistent with the sagas. The book also describes the binding of Fenris as taking place after the Viking Age, in the Dark Ages. Why would the folklore of these people describe something that hadn\u2019t happened yet as though it had already happened?<br /> <br /> I think one of the biggest missed opportunities with the Get of Fenris and reconciliation with actual Viking culture lies in Thor. Thor was clearly the popular \u201cpeople\u2019s god,\u201d and was also descended from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fj%C3%B6rgyn_and_Fj%C3%B6rgynn\" target=\"_blank\">Fj\u00f6rgyn</a>, the personification of the Earth itself. The focus should have been on how the Fenrir see the religion of their kinfolk in relation to Thor, not Odin. On the whole the entire concept is hard to reconcile, since Loki is supposed to give birth to both Fenris and Jormungandr. Somewhere between adhering to Viking culture blindly in the original edition and trying to dismantle the religion completely in revised, I feel there was probably a more elegant way to address these conflicting ideas.<br /> <br /> And by now you can tell what my favorite tribe is, most likely.<br /> <br /> The other four:<br /> - Fianna (like the Fenrir, I shared a cultural background with these people)<br /> - Wendigo (I love Native American culture, and the artistic depictions of Wendigo in any version are always awesome)<br /> - Silver Fangs (a very interesting tribe, as far as what they have to deal with, their level of responsibility, and the tragedy that plagues them. Also, Albrecht is a badass and possibly my favorite canon character.)<br /> - Glass Walkers (very much disliked them before revised, but the revised tribe book totally nailed the concept for me).<br /> <br /> Least favorite: Stargazers. They just seemed pointless and powerless, while trying to represent all of Asia somehow. I was glad to see the Shadow Lords and Glass Walkers get fleshed-out Asian cousins to fill the void left here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","user":"Viking Funeral","date":". 02-24-2016, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T02:34:47-08:00","id":836311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viking Funeral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=836274#post836274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't call them &quot;anti-Vikings,&quot; since even the Revised book makes it clear that they were involved in Viking culture.<br /> <br /> While the Revised tribebook is one of my favorites, I feel like the entire spin of Odin the Enemy Vampire was an over-reaction to the Einherjar in Dark Ages Vampire.<br /> <br /> I had to take the whole thing with a grain of salt. While it makes sense to portray Odin as the adversary of Great Fenris, since they will kill each other at Ragnarok, the same speaker also lists Loki as one of Fenris\u2019 enemies, which as far as I know is not consistent with the sagas. The book also describes the binding of Fenris as taking place after the Viking Age, in the Dark Ages. Why would the folklore of these people describe something that hadn\u2019t happened yet as though it had already happened?<br /> <br /> I think one of the biggest missed opportunities with the Get of Fenris and reconciliation with actual Viking culture lies in Thor. Thor was clearly the popular \u201cpeople\u2019s god,\u201d and was also descended from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fj%C3%B6rgyn_and_Fj%C3%B6rgynn\" target=\"_blank\">Fj\u00f6rgyn</a>, the personification of the Earth itself. The focus should have been on how the Fenrir see the religion of their kinfolk in relation to Thor, not Odin. On the whole the entire concept is hard to reconcile, since Loki is supposed to give birth to both Fenris and Jormungandr. Somewhere between adhering to Viking culture blindly in the original edition and trying to dismantle the religion completely in revised, I feel there was probably a more elegant way to address these conflicting ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you actually got what it was trying to say. Odin/Wotan in Werewolf are distinctly not tied to Vampire the Masquerade. Their history is marked by long battles with this entity, which was probably a very, very powerful Mage (I'd say embodied Spirit/God, but it looks like he is very tied to his physical form). The powers, mastery of the Umbra, magic and followers he has had through the ages are vastly beyond anything implied for the Einharjar or their dime store leader. Better yet, the entry on vampires has zilch to say about Odin.<br /> <br /> You are assuming folklore works from our perspective rather then the other way around. The Get have been using the Aesir as a good way to hide and keep up the Veil. The concept is that they wanted to create the anti-Aesir, and they did. Loki is portrayed as deceitful and playing both sides. He is not the father of Fenris, though. Thor himself is vastly overrated. He's a cool God, but he's the single most overused Nordic diety.<br /> <br /> For Werewolves who are so much different from standard religion and conceptions of reality the twist with Fenris was a stroke of genius that was only properly played with the coming of Revised. Prior to that it was just someone wanting Werewolf vikings and figuring out the Wolf God is who they should be serving.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T14:42:55-08:00","id":836691,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, the mythos in W:tA aggressively and constantly deconstructs everything humans believe about their place/level of importance in the world, which means that any given religion across history is going to get up-ended and roughed up at some point in the presentation of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T18:37:55-08:00","id":837342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=836311#post836311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you actually got what it was trying to say. Odin/Wotan in Werewolf are distinctly not tied to Vampire the Masquerade. Their history is marked by long battles with this entity, which was probably a very, very powerful Mage (I'd say embodied Spirit/God, but it looks like he is very tied to his physical form). The powers, mastery of the Umbra, magic and followers he has had through the ages are vastly beyond anything implied for the Einharjar or their dime store leader. Better yet, the entry on vampires has zilch to say about Odin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware that each game line was not bound to the mythology of the others, but reading Wolves of the Sea and then later GoF:R, I couldn't help but get the impression that the author had put himself in the box of having to explain Odin as a &quot;bad guy.&quot; I thought I had even remembered a mention in the Tribebook of Odin being a Vampire, but after cracking it open for the first time in a while, that reference doesn't exist. Memory is a funny thing.<br /> <br /> Some of the powers ascribed to Odin in GoF:R sound very much like the abilities of a powerful Kindred, and the Einherjar regard Odin as the progenitor of the vampires of the North. But your'e right, no specific reference to Odin as a vampire in GoF:R.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/810904-your-favorite-tribes-which-and-why?p=836311#post836311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are assuming folklore works from our perspective rather then the other way around. The Get have been using the Aesir as a good way to hide and keep up the Veil. The concept is that they wanted to create the anti-Aesir, and they did. Loki is portrayed as deceitful and playing both sides. He is not the father of Fenris, though. Thor himself is vastly overrated. He's a cool God, but he's the single most overused Nordic diety.<br /> <br /> For Werewolves who are so much different from standard religion and conceptions of reality the twist with Fenris was a stroke of genius that was only properly played with the coming of Revised. Prior to that it was just someone wanting Werewolf vikings and figuring out the Wolf God is who they should be serving.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, I feel like it's the writer of the Tribebook who felt we should be beholden to the folklore, and that we had to deal with the Fenris/Odin rivalry head-on. This lead to the need to spin the entire mythology. The idea that the Fenrir took advantage of this &quot;revised&quot; reality of the situation to enforce the Veil seems to be an afterthought, a throw-away reference at the end of several pages where the author tries to somehow justify Fenris being the &quot;good guy,&quot; and in doing so labels the entire Norse religion a farce. That's awfully dismissive of the people that gave rise to the legends that inspired the idea of the Get of Fenris in the first place. I was fine with a vague &quot;Viking werewolves&quot; idea, and it could have been just left at that. The paragraph following the header &quot;Legendry of the Humans&quot; on page 21 would have been a perfect starting point to just leave the concept up in the air; &quot;those ridiculous humans and their stories, they even claim Fenris was born from Loki. They don't know the truth.&quot; (Paraphrased.) The explanation of the importance of the Norse deities should have been left simple and vague, and more space should have been given to the beliefs and culture of the other Germanics who contributed to the culture of the Fenrir. The day that a Get of Fenris Tribebook writer steps outside the box of &quot;everything must be Viking&quot; and uses the concept of the Interpretatio Germanica as a means to connect the various Germanic peoples across each region and era will be a great day.<br /> <br /> When I said before that the Fenrir were involved in Viking culture, I should have said thoroughly embedded. All but one of their camps are named for members of the Aesir, or Vanir allies. Their Gifts reference many of the same. If the &quot;evil wolves as the opponents of the people's gods for the sake of the Veil&quot; angle had been more thoroughly explored, or better yet, the entire concept of the Get of Fenris to begin with, that would have been a much better way to sell &quot;Viking werewolves.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","user":"Viking Funeral","date":". 02-26-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7445-viking-funeral","name":"Viking Funeral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7445_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T01:01:03-08:00","id":837434,"title":"","content":"If Fenris is good, then Odin must be bad. What's so strange about the concept? As for invalidating human religion and mythology Werewolf does it at every corner, pretty much concluding &quot;silly humans&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:37:06-08:00","id":838833,"title":"","content":"My tastes have changed over the years, I remember loving the Get of Fenris when I first happened across WtA for their warrior culture and Viking stereotype. Afterwards I went though a xenophobic period where I wanted to keep my games in the UK and I found my tastes moving over to the Fianna. However over the last few years my heart belongs to the Bones Gnawers. I love how they are so far down the social totem pole of both the human and garou world they tend to be near invisible. I like how they are born survivors and have a sense of honour that brings up the lowest of the low and look after them. I even have a roleplaying rule I refer to as the Bone Gnawer effect where a player is based around the bottom rung of society and the rest of the group try to drag the up and even try to buy gear and clothes for them so they don't 'show them up'. I like to resist these attempts and think to legends like Dirty Frank from 2000ad who looks like shit but gets things done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T01:13:00-08:00","id":839016,"title":"","content":"That with your interests changing is pretty normal. I used to think that the Glass Walkers were the only cool Garou. With time I've really learned to love them all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T19:26:04-08:00","id":840330,"title":"","content":"1)The Fianna will always hold a special place in my heart. i love the angle where they are knowledge keepers of the garou, and as an avid fan of Changeling: The Dreaming I really enjoy the general mystical feel of the Fianna. Though I have to admit the emphasis on drinking and partying *couch*Resist Toxin*cough* is in pretty bad taste...<br /> <br /> 2) I actually enjoy the bone grawers quite a bit. I see them as the plucky underdogs (no pun intended) of the plucky underdogs that are the garou nation. you might put them down, but you can't keep them down. <br /> <br /> 3) The Black Furies are an interesting concept and one I'd love to explore in character more. In that I'd love to use the character to take a serious look at sex, gender and the role of women both in the natural world and human civilization. <br /> <br /> 4) The Children of Gaia are actually fun and pretty bad ass all around, probably the most misunderstood tribe there is both in and out of cannon IMO.<br /> <br /> 5) The Silver Fangs; sometimes its just nice to be that shining hero that everyone admires. If only...(pick any three of the myriad of internal political struggles, neurosis, external enemies, institutionalized prejudices, scarcity of resources, potential metaphysical corruptions, ect.) would stop getting in the way.<br /> <br /> Least favs.<br /> <br /> 1) The Red Talons: no mr. wolf, genocide is bad.<br /> <br /> 2) The Get of Fenris: no, mr. viking, being a better fighter does not make you right. <br /> <br /> 3) Stargazers: bad game design, espeically in second edition with the dreaded lupus ahroun combo. <br /> <br /> <br /> The others I'm usually pretty indifferent towards personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T20:07:24-08:00","id":841077,"title":"","content":"It is really hard to knock on the Apocalypse tribes. I guess the only one I kind of dislike is the 3rd Edition Fianna. Other than that, they all bring something interesting and unique to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T02:29:26-08:00","id":841183,"title":"","content":"It's not that hard to knock on the Tribes... even if they all bring something interesting and unique to the game (I would argue strenuously that they don't). I can make pretty solid cases for most of the Tribes, even ones I like, adding far more bad to the game than they do good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T06:23:26-08:00","id":841262,"title":"","content":"Well, chocolate makes you fat, it doesn't mean it isn't delicious!<br /> <br /> Everything and everyone have their flaws, and most of them, when it comes to RPGs, are in the eye of the beholder, so its all well and good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T14:51:17-08:00","id":843146,"title":"","content":"I dig the <b>Fianna </b>because they're fighting to live, not living to fight, and that's a much saner point of view than a lot of tribes have on the Apocalypse war.<br /> <br /> My first character was one of the <b>Children of Gaia</b>, so natch they hold a special place for me. I dig that they're stepping back and taking a big picture view.<br /> <br /> The <b>Glass Walkers</b> are just goddamn neat, no two ways about it. Cybershamans communing with electro spirits and LMG-toting Ahrouns are too cool not to love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T09:15:06-07:00","id":865972,"title":"","content":"This List is very uninformed, as I sadly am just now going to play the game. Still rather familiar with the fluff, so I guess that counts a little? Ranking is mainly based on the W20 corebook Version.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Children of Gaia<br /> I like their sane, humanistic approach and their willingness to Show restraint while being no less badass than the other tribes. Always saw them more in the veine of &quot;Technical Pacifists&quot; like Kenshin: not out for bloodshed, but very able to kick ass if necessary. Somehow Missed the Hippie vibe at first, though in retrospect seems obvious.Playing one would be just like fishmalks to me: kinda Fun here and there, but ultimately missing the point.<br /> 2. Bone Gnawers <br /> LOVE the underdog, survival-first, practical theme permeating them. Most people already put their appeal more eloquently than I could.<br /> 3. Glass Walters<br /> Technogifts. Need I say more?<br /> 4. White Howlers<br /> Something about them is just very fascinating to me. Maybe the tragedy?<br /> 5.<br /> Not sure, I guess Fianna and Silver Fangs sharing the spot.<br /> <br /> Dislike<br /> 1. Black Furies<br /> Somehow Irks me. Like the concept, but the execution Kind of irritates me.<br /> 2. Shadow Lords<br /> Dislike is maybe too strong a term, just not interested all that much in them.<br /> 3. Red Talon<br /> Appears to be very flat. Maybe it's my lack of experience though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 04-15-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:52:01-07:00","id":866062,"title":"","content":"My tastes have super changed over time, but it seems like they're in line with a lot of other people.<br /> In no particular order:<br /> 1) Shadow Lords, when being heroic. They are the competent ones, they know how to lead, and they really do have the nation's best interests at heart. Yeah you have to break a few eggs, but you don't have to be happy about it. That, and internal tribe politics are kind of neat. Lots of good RP opportunities within the tribe, and not all of them are pure deceit.<br /> 2) Silver Fangs, when being heroic. They have unique abilities to bring people together, and I think those are often underplayed or played wrong. Other tribebooks don't give them nearly enough the respect that I think individuals would. When they're not being incompetent dicks, and the tribe members really are properly educated in how to be a good leader, they can deserve the respect they expect. They have to work super hard and push themselves to never fail, not even a little bit; that kind of inner conflict works a lot better than &quot;okay they're brain damaged how tragic&quot;. Needs good players in the whole pack to really do the dynamic right though, and it's pretty easy to fall into &quot;oh okay the sept leader is a fang, bow to the fang, who's a good plot device, you are, you are&quot;.<br /> 3) Glass Walkers, in plots that push rationality a little too far. If anyone's going to save the Garou Nation and win the war, it is absolutely these guys, even if they lose a bit of their soul in the process. Great second-in-commands handling logistics for any powerful leader, because sentiment and tradition is what's really killing the nation these days, not infighting. I love these guys setting up humane and unoppressive eugenics programs. They get a bad rap for being out of touch with their wyld nature, but it seems like they and their kinfolk are always the ones who carry the load when it comes to protecting others' natural habitats. Yes, that's great Mr. Wendigo that you're in touch with nature in your vast tracts of land. Who do you think is keeping humans from fracking or logging that land? It's not your guys attacking their heavy machinery, it's the Walkers buying companies out or forging geological data. The danger with Walkers is if you make them the only people who ever do that, because it's not like the Furies don't have politicians or hackers or whatever, but the Walkers are still the ones who plan on the largest scale for the whole nation, and they're the ones you run to when the shit hits the fan, or when you need to head off a future attack on a caern. Also...it's fun to see their take on rites. My favorite character stared at a random number generator as a divination tool. Maybe it's just easier to identify with them.<br /> 4) Children of Gaia, when playing against stereotype. Coggies can be mean SOBs. Everyone wants a Coggie Ahroun who's not afraid to murder the hell out of people. Also good when they resolve conflicts without being fluffy bunnies. A good Child of Gaia who has a terrifying force of personality and can really back it up with force, while still remaining impartial, is a real benefit for the nation.<br /> 5) Wendigo, when scary as hell and not holding back. Oh god, get out of their way. Sometimes they get cast as the crying Indian who needs to be saved from the mean wyrmcomers and I think that's a huge disservice.<br /> <br /> Least favorite:<br /> Bone Gnawers. I just can't find the interest. Never have. I think this is a matter of my personal opinion never matching up with the way they're played. They oughtta be looked down on for good reason, not just because they keep trying to bum change off of you. This may be unjustified on my part. IMO a lot more conflict-with-other-werewolves plots should be &quot;damn it, it's the Gnawers' fault that everything went to hell, AGAIN&quot;. Instead it's usually the SLords who eat that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:10:09-07:00","id":867808,"title":"","content":"My least favorite hands down has always been the Red Talons. On the surface they always struck me as flat despite having a interesting concept. They come across less as a Tribe of Wolves and more as the bitter, angry Anti-Human Tribe. Maybe their Tribebook makes them more interesting but just way they've been handled in the Rulebooks and some of the other books I have read, saps any interest I have in reading the Tribebook.<br /> <br /> Favorite tribe, originally the Glass Walkers but in recent years I've become more and more interested in the White Howlers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T14:28:22-07:00","id":871734,"title":"","content":"My favorites but I think all the tribes can be awesome if they are used in cool ways so I like them all, but enough cop out<br /> Favorites;<br /> 1. Fianna; This probably relates to my Irish descent, but I really like the feel of the Fianna tribe and the idea of these Celtic warrior-poets and being record keepers of the Garou, I'm a bit upset it seems so many people don't seem to like them but, hey to each their own I guess<br /> 2.Get of Fenris; These guys are just so awesome to me, I love Norse mythology and as we all know everything is better with Vikings. Plus with their rage I feel their the closest tribe to the traditional Feral,Beast Werewolf that we see.<br /> 3. Bonegnawers;I just think that these guys are so cool. The kind of scrappy omega's of the Garou nation who dedicate themselves to the protection of Humanity's weakest elements. Downtrodden and looked on with disgust but being one of the most adapted tribes to the modern world and arguably the most adept City-Garou.<br /> 4.Wendigo; I think I might just have a thing for Warrior tribes and the Wendigo rival the Get Warrior wise for me. The themes of Cold and their unrelenting rage together in the Wendigo make them one of my favorite tribes theme wise.<br /> 5.Black furies; This tribe is also really cool for me, with it's connection to the Wyld, Greek mythos(which I love) and being the best Girl Power faction that White Wolf ever made in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Least Favorite(1 being Worst-5 being least worst)<br /> 1. Glasswalkers; the reason the glasswalkers are here is I feel they just feel out of place among the Garou and they just never appealed to me.<br /> 2. Stargazers; another tribe that just never hit my interests and really did belong more in the beast courts, plus the odd surplus of Lupus Ahroun in their tribe.Weird.<br /> 3. Children of Gaia; I can see this tribe being cool but White Wolf just did not help these poor guys, I can see uses for them but they just feel dull for me.<br /> 4. Silent Striders; I think that the whole settite connection and wanderer thing is cool but I could never think of any more use for them then an occasional visit of a strider to the caern.<br /> 5. Red talons; Now for me I feel these guys get to much hate, in my games their more hardcore Wyld , then the borderline Wyrm stereotype, but it's true that they simply don't mix well with homids or stories involving human and that's why there here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:09:19-07:00","id":875284,"title":"","content":"Just werewolf tribes, i have always liked<br /> 1) bone gnawers, i have always loved underdogs<br /> 2) glass walkers, one of the more humanistic tribes, plus some of their fetishes/talens are just cool (such as the John woo clips)<br /> 3) Stargazers, cause i like the mysticism<br /> 4) Silent striders, cause i just like their backstory<br /> <br /> Now if we can add in other Fera, i would rank Mokole and Gurhal as higher than Garou (if allowed), and Bastet just under Garou. Never played a Corax, Ratkin, Sharkman or Nuwisha, and have yet to find a ST willing to allow Anassi.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T06:06:07-07:00","id":1398592,"title":"","content":"1 SILVER FANGS: I remember being just a teenager and the first time I opened the Dark ages book I wondered about this tribe. They had all I wanted, the power, the tragedy of the Harano, the glory and the respect of all other tribes, very powerful gifts and an interesting Russian background and culture who was very original in the american games.<br /> <br /> 2 SILENT STRIDERS: But now, my tastes have evolved to something different. 15 years later, I find this tribe the most interesting. They are mysterious, powerful wizards, they have a different tragedy, that being banished from their land and it offers some cool ideas of crossover with vampire and wraith. This elusive, independent and mystic tribe is one of my favorites.<br /> <br /> 3 BONE GNAWERS: They are the underdog, survivalists, they have some sense of humor and they are progressive and egalitarian, in contrast with the nobility of the Fangs. This could have been my favorite tribe if not for the american focus of the revised book, who turn my initial attraction to distaste. They have become the new american tribe, the american dreamers, the american independents, the american social fighters... america, america, america, so boring.<br /> <br /> However, the tribe who I would not like to play at all are the GLASS WALKERS. Werewolf hackers and mafiosos? Their totem is a crocroach, c\u00b4mon! What else? I think it is disconnected from the main setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 06-24-2020, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T09:04:54-07:00","id":1398609,"title":"","content":"1. Children of Gaia - Neutral diplomats who embrace from my understanding the: &quot;Force is the method when everything else failed.&quot; stance.<br /> 2. Glasswalkers - Those that want to be more in reach to their human kinfolks and try to bring the change from within.<br /> 3. Shadowlords - because those are the stealth fighters that act on &quot;The end justify the means.&quot;<br /> 4. Fianna - Because they have connections to fay and are great celebrators and fighters<br /> 5. Bone Gnawers - Because they represent the underdogs and bring change from the other stand of people that would be most likely to be corrupted.<br /> <br /> 3. Black Furies - While I can understand their cause and think it is important I suffered from those that took it to far (and would be called Feminazis) so I as a player have the opinion, that it is already enough or it will turn to the other point of inequality.<br /> 2. Silver Fangs - Degenerates from an ended age. Leaders should not be because of Blood but of Skill (and I honestly never really understood the true breed thing)<br /> 1. Red Talons - They are for me just extremists that because of their blind rage can not see the truth of the actual world","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T10:51:14-07:00","id":1398621,"title":"","content":"1: Silent Striders - I am a sucker for the slightly mysterious lone wanderer.<br /> 2: Get of Fenris - I am Danish<br /> 3: Glass Walkers - Not sure why, maybe because they are so different, but I just really like 'em.<br /> 4: Wendigo, courtesy of Wyld West and a great campaign my wife ran.<br /> 5: Actually not sure...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T04:10:40-07:00","id":1399006,"title":"","content":"Well, this looks like a Resurrection. <br /> <br /> I like all the tribes. think it's not so much 'least favourite tribe' as much as 'Which tribe do you love to hate?&quot; <br /> <br /> Favourites: <br /> <br /> 1- Get. <br /> You see these tribes? This one goes to 11. I will out-garou your garou. Tribe members are proven family and everyone else can fuck off. Rage ratings lower than 5 need not apply. <br /> 2 Bone Gnawers<br /> Capturing the Wyld of the city, class struggle embodyment, Ratkin buddies? Gold (metaphorically, lord knows they don't have any physical gold) <br /> 3- Glass Walkers<br /> Money, Cybernetics, power armour, 20mm Autocannons; If I didn't imagine half of them with neon hair dye they'd take No.1 <br /> <br /> 4- Shadow lords<br /> Smart wolf is best wolf. Calculating characters are fun to play. <br /> <br /> 5- BSD<br /> A film is often carried by the quality of it's villain. BSD's make great villains and there's a lot of room to do what you want with them. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Love to hate: <br /> 1-Children of Gaia; Tribe hypocrite. Look at how I love the Get, these guys are the opposite. I hope they never change. <br /> 2- Fianna. <br /> World class bullshitters. Really cool bullshit though. <br /> <br /> 3-BF: Bunch of misandrist TERFs. Really cool gifts and mythology. I hope they never change. <br /> 4- Silver fangs: <br /> Greatest of station eh? Well, who am I to argue with you? look at that splendid coat of yours! <br /> <br /> <br /> I got this far and thought it unfair. I love silent striders but at the same time their lack of a home and the fact they don't play great with others hampers them a bit, Stargazers are pulpy fun but they don't carry the core themes well.. Uktena are cool but they're less-cool shadow lords to me. (In some ways they're more cool, but on the whole they're not as good.) <br /> <br /> I think wendigo need work, Red talons could be a lot better (also these two tribes have a few really cool gifts but mostly have mediocrity)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T21:06:46-07:00","id":1399492,"title":"","content":"I like them all for different reasons. The Silent Striders are probably my favorite because I have a private reason for extreme personal bias. I think if asked to pick three others, they'd be the Shadow Lords (because sometimes ruthless pragmatism is a lot of fun), Glass Walkers (because there are certain personally amusing tropes I can do with them that don't work so well with other tribes), and Fianna (there are certain cultural tropes I enjoy playing around with).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T23:01:25-07:00","id":1399514,"title":"","content":"Favourites:<br /> <br /> 1)Black Furies.<br /> <br /> 2) Older Brother.<br /> <br /> 3) Red Talons.<br /> <br /> 4) Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> 5) CoGs.<br /> <br /> Least favs.<br /> <br /> 1) Silver Fangs.<br /> <br /> 2) Fianna.<br /> <br /> 3) Shadow Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T22:05:11-07:00","id":1480927,"title":"","content":"My chosen tribes are:<br /> <br /> 1 Silent striders: I like the mysterious solitaire wanderers and occultists.<br /> <br /> 2 Bone gnawers: Playing the underdog, the freemen, the nomad, the highwaymen is appealing.<br /> <br /> 3 Silver fangs: Fallen nobility, old sagas crippling under anachronic feudalism and propension to harano.<br /> <br /> 4 Shadow lords: Cunning, astute schemers and pol\u00edticos.<br /> <br /> 5 Children of Gaia or Fianna: These tribes are the core of the game, in my opinion. The werewolf as a barbarian mystical shapeshifter and the werewolf as a defender of the nature and the ecology.<br /> <br /> <br /> I do not like the racial stuff of the tribes, so Wendigo, Fenrir or Fianna have issues for me for this reason, and also all the shapeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T05:54:39-07:00","id":1481172,"title":"","content":"Red Talons, Children of Gaian, Get of Fenris<br /> <br /> Least: the native american ones. I think they're boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-15T22:25:58-07:00","id":1481214,"title":"","content":"In no particular order:<br /> <br /> Get of Fenris<br /> I like Vikings and Norse tropes and/or stereotypes. They go great with many werewolf themes, so the GoF may well be the most thematic of the Tribes in my opinion. In many ways, they personify werewolves as a culture of warriors. It will suck if we lose them.<br /> <br /> Silver Fangs<br /> I like the fallen nobility aspect of this tribe. The nobility, the madness, the sense of superiority combined with failures and flaws. I find them to be very complex from a role playing perspective.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers<br /> Like the Get of Fenris, the BSD personify certain aspects of werewolves, but it is the dark and no steroid qualities. They are monsters. They are horrifying. They are sick and twisted, removed from mortal society and Garou society alike. They are the dark mirror held up to every werewolf representing the monstrous aspect of their race. <br /> <br /> Uktena<br /> If the Get of Fenris personify the berserker warrior aspect of Garou society, then the Uktena represent the mystical aspects of it. They have Native American style spirituality and traditions with less racial baggage than the Wendigo, they are experts of the spirit worlds and mystical knowledge, they have some measure of moral complexity in their dealing with dark spirits. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure about a 5th tribe. Maybe Shadow Lords, because I like the fact that they are schemers and manipulators, it makes them a bit different than the rest of the more ideological tribes, or the Fianna because I like Celtic myths, legends, and style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T12:02:45-07:00","id":1481311,"title":"","content":"Don't really have much experience with Werewolf, so in a lot of ways this list is probably influenced as much or more by what people have said here on the forums than on actual play-time, but here goes. I can't really sort them into a neat tier-list from favourite to least, so my top five are going to be sorted alphabetically rather than ranked numerically.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: My preferred choice for the city-wolves. Pragmatism, solidarity, and class struggle themes? Sounds great to me! Also cool that they are city-wolves without making that their main identity, but rather just an extension of their pragmatism.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: I like the contrast between the violent nature of the Garou with the conscious choice to embrace peace, inclusiveness, and solidarity as much as possible; gives me a bit of a Paarthurnax vibe. They seem like one of the groups of Garou that are relatively more aware that you can't beat the literal embodiment of destruction and corruption by trying to destroy it with brute force. I've heard their source material is a bit cringe, but my broad-strokes knowledge means that I just get to look at the base concept, which I dig.<br /> <br /> Silent Striders: Nomadism and necromancy (like &quot;talking to ghosts&quot; necromancy, not &quot;arise zombie minions!&quot; necromancy), neat stuff IMO! I Also interesting for having a particular cultural/geographic root that remains influential while still being able to move far beyond that and adapt.<br /> <br /> Stargazers: Kind of the same as the CoG, I like the fact that they represent Garou consciously working to overcome the downsides of their Rage. I really like them having a more philosophical and inquisitive approach.<br /> <br /> Uktena: Magic and mysticism tend to be one of my favourite things, so them being the Tribe that focuses most on the Umbra and Spirits makes them very interesting to me, along with their penchant for trying to uncover occult lore, including sometimes meddling with Things Garou Weren't Meant to Know.<br /> <br /> <br /> Partly because I wanted to try and stick to a limit of five, and partly because my feelings here are more complicated, I wanted to make special mention regarding the Red Talons. Their mainstream culture and philosophy is not something I'm a fan of, aside from the potential as a Villain (Protagonist), and even then I find the lack of nuance uninteresting. But I actually have a lot of fun with my personal ideas about what I think the Red Talons *should* be as opposed to what they *are*, and the idea that the Tribe as it exists now has effectively &quot;fallen from grace&quot; and forgotten the role they really should be playing in the Garou Nation. So the idea of playing what is a effectively a Drizzt for the Red Talons, the rebel against their asshole culture, is one that I find really intriguing. I think the big flaw with that idea is that their biases are shared by their Tribal Totem, which means that being a Red Talon who rejects their genocidal speciesism would be almost impossible without getting yourself thrown out of the Tribe for failing to gut a human because they looked at a tree the wrong way.<br /> <br /> In one sense, my least favourite Tribe is probably the Silver Fangs. Mostly because I've become pretty staunchly anti-aristocracy, so the idea of playing a member of an entire Tribe of them does not interest me especially. But I don't necessarily dislike them as part of the lore, just probably wouldn't want to play them generally.<br /> <br /> I'd say the only Tribes I have a particular dislike for are the ones where half or more of their entire identity can be reduced to &quot;[ethnic identiy] werewolves!&quot; So the Fianna, Get of Fenris, and Wendigo. The Tribes themselves are essentially their own ethnic identities, and having them neatly map onto very particular human cultures is uninteresting to me, and kind of lazy. I don't care what IC justifications they have for it, the OOC decisions were made first, and they were lazy and uninteresting decisions IMO.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;ethnic identity werewolves&quot; would make more sense as sub-groups within different Tribes that are above and beyond human borders. So, for example, the Get might make an interesting subgroup of the Silver Fangs, Viking werewolves that think their alpha status in the Garou Nation is derived from their strength. Only problem is that making those groups into sub-factions would then make their existing sub-factions either minutely small or non-existent, which would probably bother their fans.<br /> <br /> Uktena get a pass both because they have consciously expanded beyond one particular ethnic group to some extent, and because their other themes are ones that really interest me. But I must admit that the way they have opened up specifically to non-European pagan cultures does run afoul of a tendency I've noticed among White Wolf, where groups that specialize in spirits and the Umbra are almost always lumped into non-European ethnicities (see: Dreamspeakers, various non-European changelings having Umbral connections thrown on as the way to make them different).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-21T22:06:42-07:00","id":1481641,"title":"","content":"According to my count, here are the current votes for favorite, not counting least favorites.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers 18<br /> Glass Walkers 18<br /> Silver Fangs 17.5<br /> Shadow Lords 15.5<br /> Get of Fenris 15<br /> Children of Gaia 13.5<br /> Uktena 11.5<br /> Fianna 11.5<br /> Black Furies 8<br /> Red Talons 8<br /> Silent Striders 8<br /> Stargazers 6.5<br /> Wendigo 4<br /> White Howlers 3<br /> Black Spiral Dancers 2<br /> <br /> Fera 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T12:22:46-07:00","id":1482278,"title":"","content":"I don't think I posted here before and not going to verify now.<br /> <br /> My top 5, ordered by Sergeant's current ranking 'cause it's easy:<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gnawers</b> - Love 'em for their better notion of the actual plight and lives of the downtrodden, the majority of human population.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Gaia</b> - Instead of using BS arguments to justify taking sides and simplifying their view of the world, they accept the truth for what it is, that everyone deserves better and no hate is justified. They may not be always able to live to their ideals, but they have the right ones instead of the cool ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies</b> - They're complex, nuanced, inconsistent as a society just as societies really are, they accept that this is normal. On top of that, as much as other tribes say they don't particularly lean to any form of sexism, they're actually the only regular source of female characters at all both in most tables and as known NPCs. They <i>exist</i> isn't the same as they being as common as they should.<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Striders</b> - Haunted wanderers that are not white by default and bring ghosts to the game? It's a hard choice between them and the Uktena, but the SS win in the end.<br /> <br /> <b>Stargazers</b> - I like their philosophy and mysticism. It is sad that they're so Asian-Coded, I don't mind it being less &quot;culture-locked&quot;, but otherwise I love them.<br /> <br /> Least interesting:<br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons</b> - While I can buy into the argument that they're less &quot;think like wolves&quot; and more &quot;think like humans trying to think like what they think wolves are like&quot;, I still see this one as <i><b>extremely</b></i> simplistic and unappealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:31:39-07:00","id":1482626,"title":"","content":"Black spiral dancers - becouse they are the only one, who understood the place of Garou. And they are trying to change ecerything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}